  "title": "Erdős Problem #619",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "For a triangle-free graph $G$ let $h_r(G)$ be the smallest number of edges that need to be added to $G$ so that it has diameter $r$ (while preserving the property of being triangle-free).\nIs it true that there exists a constant $c>0$ such that if $G$ is a connected graph on $n$ vertices then $h_4(G)<(1-c)n$?",
